WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:01.860
- [Instructor] In this video,
we're gonna think about

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.470
how we can use our knowledge

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:07.640
of multiplying single digit
numbers to multiply things

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.610
that might involve two digits.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:14.453
So for example, let's start
with, what is five times 18?

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:18.130
And you can pause the video
and see how you might try

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:20.530
to approach this, and
then we'll do it together.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.290
All right, so if we're trying
to tackle five times 18,

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:30.290
one strategy could be to
say, hey, can I re-express 18

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.850
as the product of two numbers?

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.220
And the one that jumps
out at me is that 18

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.810
is the same thing as two times nine,

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:43.130
and so I could rewrite five times 18.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:46.050
This is the same thing as five

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:51.050
times, instead of 18, I
can write two times nine.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.230
Now, why does this help us?

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:58.470
Well, instead of multiplying
the two times nine first

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.540
to get the 18, and then
multiplying that by five,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.820
what we could do is we
could multiply the five

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:06.330
times the two first.

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.850
And you might be thinking,
wait, wait, wait,

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:08.970
hold on a second.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:12.300
Before, you did the two times nine first,

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.500
and now, you're telling me

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.210
that you're going to change the order?

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.180
That you're going to say, hey,

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.940
let's multiply the five times
two first, is that okay?

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.230
And the simple answer is, yes, it is okay.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.750
If you are multiplying
a string of numbers,

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.620
you can do them in any
order that you choose,

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.870
and so this is often known

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:32.140
as the associative
property of multiplication.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:35.250
We can associate the
two with the nine first.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.830
We can multiply those first,

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:40.630
or we can have an association
with the five and the two.

00:01:40.630 --> 00:01:42.630
We can multiply those two first.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:44.610
Now, why is that helpful?

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.810
Well, what is five times two?

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.110
Well, that's pretty straightforward.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:49.800
That's going to be equal to 10.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.360
So this is going to be equal to 10.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:55.530
We're doing that same color.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.893
10 times nine.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:01.150
Now, 10 times nine is a
lot more straightforward

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:03.890
for most of us than five times 18.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.190
10 times nine is equal to 90.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:09.010
Let's do another example.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:14.010
Let's say we wanna figure
out what three times 21 is.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.330
Pause this video and see if
you can work through that.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.020
There's multiple ways to do it,

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.100
but see if you can do it the way

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.483
we just approached this first example.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:26.940
Well, as you could image,
we want to re-express 21

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.810
as the product of smaller numbers.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:34.270
So we could rewrite 21 as
three times seven maybe?

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:38.000
And so if we rewrite it
as three times seven,

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.900
and now, we do the
three times three first.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:43.270
So I'm just gonna put parenthesis
there, which we can do

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.580
because the associative
property of multiplication.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:46.700
Fancy word for something

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.020
that is hopefully a little bit intuitive.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.430
Well then, this is going to be equal to,

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:52.720
what's three times three?

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.200
It is nine,

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:58.540
and then times seven,
which you may already know

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:02.510
is equal to 63.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:03.440
Let's do another example.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.390
This is kinda fun.

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:09.640
Let's say we wanna figure
out what 14 times five is.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.093
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.960
Well, we could once
again try to break up 14

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:17.830
into the product of smaller numbers.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.610
14 is two times seven,

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:23.320
so we can rewrite this as two times seven

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.020
or as seven times two,

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.540
and I'm writing it as seven times two,

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.010
because I want to associate
the two with the five

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.730
to get the 10 times five,

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.970
and then I can multiply
the two times five first.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:40.970
And so this is going to
give us seven times 10,

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:46.380
seven times 10, which is
of course equal to 70.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:48.490
One more example.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:53.460
Let's say we want to
calculate 15 times three.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:54.760
How would you tackle that?

00:03:55.690 --> 00:04:00.510
Well, we can break up 15
into five times three.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.540
Five times three,

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.980
and then we can multiply that,
of course, by this three,

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.570
and then we can multiply
the threes together first,

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:12.820
and then this amounts to five times nine.

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.770
And five times nine,

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:17.110
you might already be familiar with this.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:20.550
This is going to be equal to 45.

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.600
Another way to get to
45, you can say, hey,

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:24.970
five times 10 is 50.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:27.590
So five times 9 is going
to be five less than that,

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:29.653
which is also 45.

